semantic_diff: >-
  Text-only fix of three lines the update-reviewer flagged as LOW notes on
  2026-09-15 against revision 11. No node, outcome, edge, check, role, evidence
  path, or state field changes; the skeleton is identical - 22 nodes, 68 edges,
  68 outcomes, 17 checks, 24 evidence, 5 control nodes, state.required and every
  role list equal, proved by parsing both graphs (/tmp/vt/rev12/make_v13.py).
  Diff: 3 hunks, 5 added lines against 5 removed; 2336 lines stay 2336.

  (1) design_campaign, check narrow_delta_scoped (line 285): "with the
  kickoff-declared criteria digest unchanged" becomes "with the kickoff-declared
  criteria unchanged (value-level read against the kickoff record)". No digest
  of the registration record exists anywhere - run-state comparator_registrations
  holds artifact and committed_at only, and references/artifact-layout.md 4.5
  pins the record as subject plus timestamp, write-once. The check's own last
  sentence already demands the value-level read; the new words name the read the
  check already requires. Same meaning: a narrow repair must not rewrite the
  criteria. Revision 7 (revisions.yaml, the kept-digest list) kept this digest as
  a write-once subject; this revision supersedes that keep-list entry for this
  site because the digest was never stored - no schema field or record holds it.

  (2) control_nodes.run_paused (lines 2215-2216): the sentence "A run that
  closes in this condition records terminal classification incomplete." is
  removed. Revision 10 renamed terminal_classification to final_status and
  missed this copy. No enum value fits: schemas/run-state.schema.json
  final_status.status allows accepted, blocked, closed_unaccepted, null, and its
  description says status mirrors the terminal_status values the graph's control
  nodes declare and is null while the run is paused; incomplete is a pave-spec
  9.13 status that no control node of this graph declares; closed_unaccepted
  belongs to run_aborted and requires the user's verbatim reason; blocked means
  no declared route remains, and a pause has one - resume. A pause node closes
  nothing (pave-spec control-node table: suspend the run and preserve resumable
  state), and the graph declares no edge from run_paused to a terminal, so the
  sentence was prose handling an undeclared route (evolution contract rule 2).
  The duty it hinted at - a walked-away run must not stay active - already lives
  in skills/vllm-neuron-parity/SKILL.md ("If you walk away from a run, set the
  final status or remove the state"). Cutting the sentence removes the phantom
  value and adds nothing. If the user later wants abandoned runs recorded as
  such, that is a graph-plus-schema change (a terminal node with terminal_status
  incomplete and the matching enum value), not a text fix.

  (3) prepare_host, outcome host_ready (line 1514): "capacity is settled per job
  by its job lease, never here" becomes "capacity is decided per job by its job
  lease, never here". The same outcome text two lines above (workflow.pave.yaml:1511)
  already says "decided by the lease record"; one verb for one idea. Same meaning.

  Every copy: one release-layer copy existed - skills/vllm-neuron-parity/SKILL.md:170
  said "run_paused (resumable; a run that closes here records final status
  incomplete)"; it is corrected to "run_paused (resumable)" in 1.5.8 alongside
  this revision, the package's precedent (revision 7: release-layer copies
  corrected in the release, the revision is the graph copy). Outside that line,
  history/, and the append-only revisions.yaml, the three old wordings occur
  nowhere else - references, schemas, hooks, tests, and the Codex port searched.
  Usage evidence: the predecessors'
  usage records (v10 usage read - 291 lease records, 0 acquire-seat traversals)
  were answered by revision 11; this revision changes no seat and the records
  ask for nothing more. Layer test (pave-spec 2.1): description text of one
  check, one outcome, and one control node - kind graph; no runtime binding
  touched.
user_only_changes: none
